  "god": {
    "combineDesks": false,
    "embodiedVerdicts": true,
    "authoring": "villager",
    "godPrompt": "Defense outpost. An ARCHER (Aldric) and a SWORDSMAN (Bertrand) must learn to DETECT hostile mobs and KILL them WITHOUT taking a single point of damage. Teach skills ONE AT A TIME, in the order below; propose ONLY the current skill's task and do NOT propose the next until the current one is admitted to the library as `active` AND confirmed by a successful verdict.\n\nThe villagers ALREADY carry full iron armor, an iron sword, a bow and arrows — do NOT propose acquiring gear. Every skill must COMPOSE the existing primitive skills (find-high-spot, go-to, shoot-mob, kill-mob, defend-self, pickup-drops) via ctx.skills.run — never re-implement a primitive. The OPERATOR builds a small tower next to the archer and places a zombie spawner within aggro range; do NOT summon mobs yourself — the spawner provides them.\n\nThe SUCCESS BAR for every combat skill is strict: the targeted mobs die AND the villager takes ZERO damage (its health never drops). A villager that gets hit has NOT succeeded — your critique must push it to engage SOONER, from FARTHER, or from HIGHER ground (and the archer must never leave its perch).\n\nThe skills to teach, in this order:\n1. perch-high (Aldric) — find the highest standable spot nearby by composing 'find-high-spot', then climb onto it with 'go-to'. The archer fights from up here so melee mobs can never reach it. GRACEFUL: if no higher spot exists, stay put and return success.\n2. snipe-hostiles (Aldric) — from the perch, LOOP: find the nearest hostile mob (e.g. a zombie) and shoot it dead with the bow by composing 'shoot-mob', repeating until none remain in range. NEVER descend the tower; take zero damage. GRACEFUL: if no hostile is in range, return success (nothing to shoot).\n3. intercept-hostiles (Bertrand) — LOOP: find the nearest hostile mob and kill it by composing 'kill-mob' (or soften it first with 'shoot-mob' while it is still far), engaging at the EDGE of detection so it dies BEFORE it can land a hit, repeating until none remain. Take zero damage. GRACEFUL: if no hostile is in range, return success.\n\nGraceful degradation (nothing to do = return success) is a SUCCESS, not a failure. Each skill is its own standalone library skill — do NOT bundle them into one big loop. After these three are active and confirmed, the mission is COMPLETE — stop proposing new skills."
  },

